## 9.1 Shared Animation Attributes

Use a consistent and maintainable marker architecture.

Possible examples:

```html
data-dandy-entrance
data-dandy-reveal
data-dandy-stagger
data-dandy-reveal-child
```

Use the markers consistently and document their meaning.

Avoid fragile selectors based on:

- Arabic text content.
- Product names.
- Arbitrary CSS class combinations.
- Page-specific element positions.

Use semantic component markers.

## 9.2 BaseLayout Integration

Evaluate whether the shared entrance controller can be initialized once through the existing BaseLayout.

If possible, initialize the shared controller globally while allowing page-specific elements to opt into reveal behavior through deliberate markers.

Do not wrap every page in unnecessary additional DOM containers.

Do not introduce nested `<main>` elements.

Do not break existing Astro layouts or page structure.

## 9.3 Existing GSAP System

Inspect:

`src/utils/animations.ts`

If the current DANDY animation controller already contains suitable reveal functionality:

- Extend it.
- Reuse existing utilities.
- Avoid duplicate ScrollTrigger instances.
- Avoid duplicate initialization.
- Ensure proper cleanup where appropriate.

If CSS and IntersectionObserver are sufficient, prefer the simpler implementation.

Do not use GSAP merely for effects that simple CSS can achieve.

